# Doctor — audit and repair dirty `.issueflows/` folders (`/iflow-doctor`)

`/iflow-doctor` checks the local issue-tracking tree for **dirty** conditions
(multiple focus groups, leftovers in `{{ current_issues_folder }}/`, duplicates
across folders, and similar) and can apply **safe repairs** on confirmation.

This is an **off-path** command — `/iflow` never auto-runs it.

{% include "skills/_model_directive.md.j2" %}

{% include "skills/_resolve_project_root.md.j2" %}

## Input

- **(nothing)** — audit only; report findings.
- **`fix`** — after presenting findings, run repair (preview with `--dry-run`
  via CLI when available).

## Steps

> **CLI fast path (optional).** If the `issue-flow` CLI is on `PATH`:
> - Audit: `issue-flow doctor [--json]` or `issue-flow agent audit`.
> - Repair: `issue-flow doctor --fix [--except N] [--dry-run] [--json]` or
>   `issue-flow agent repair`.
>
> Fallback: `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ designs_folder }}/dirty-issueflows.md`.

1. Resolve `<project_root>` and run the audit.

2. Present findings grouped by severity (`error`, `warn`, `info`).

3. If the user asked for repair (or confirms after audit), run repair with
   `--dry-run` first when moves are planned; require `--except N` when focus is
   ambiguous.

4. Re-audit and summarize.

5. **Housekeeping commit (default when issueflows-only dirty).** Doctor repair
   never runs `git commit`. After a successful repair, if
   `issue-flow agent preflight --json` (or `git status --porcelain`) shows a
   dirty tree whose paths are **all** under `{{ issueflows_dir }}/`, list them,
   propose
   `chore: doctor housekeeping — archive/sweep {{ issueflows_dir }} groups`,
   and ask for **one confirm** (recommended: yes). On yes: stage **only** those
   paths and commit — **no push**. On mixed dirt (any path outside
   `{{ issueflows_dir }}/`), report and do not offer this default.

## Constraints

- Never delete issue markdown or merge duplicate groups automatically.
- Never auto-dispatch `/iflow-doctor` from `/iflow`, `/iflow-build`, or
  `/iflow-close`.
- Repair moves need explicit user confirmation.
- Never auto-commit from the CLI; agent commits only after the step-5 confirm.

## Output

Short sections: **Findings**, **Repair plan** (if applicable), **Result**,
**Housekeeping commit** (if applicable).
